","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution/error state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncThrottler"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Awaited"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReturnType"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Throttle an async API call\nconst handleApiCall = useAsyncThrottledCallback(async (data) => {\n  const result = await sendDataToServer(data);\n  return result;\n}, {\n  wait: 200 // Execute at most once every 200ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event handler\n<button onClick={() => handleApiCall(formData)}>Send</button>","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncThrottledCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-throttler/useAsyncThrottledCallback.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/async-throttler/useAsyncThrottledCallback.ts#L43)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a throttled version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncThrottler` hook,\nproviding a stable, throttled async function reference for use in Preact components.\n\nThe throttled async function will execute at most once within the specified wait time period,\nregardless of how many times it is called. Calls made during the wait period reschedule a\nsingle trailing execution with the latest arguments when `trailing` is enabled (the default).\nThe most recent call's promise resolves or rejects with the trailing execution's result;\neach earlier call's promise resolves immediately with the most recent previous result (or\n`undefined` if nothing has executed yet), as does every call when the throttler is disabled.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncThrottler`, making it ideal for basic\nasync throttling needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncThrottler instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution/error state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncThrottler` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Throttle an async API call\nconst handleApiCall = useAsyncThrottledCallback(async (data) => {\n  const result = await sendDataToServer(data);\n  return result;\n}, {\n  wait: 200 // Execute at most once every 200ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event handler\n<button onClick={() => handleApiCall(formData)}>Send</button>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncThrottledCallback\ntitle: useAsyncThrottledCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncThrottledCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-throttler/useAsyncThrottledCallback.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/preact-pacer/src/async-throttler/useAsyncThrottledCallback.ts#L43)\n\nA Preact hook that creates a throttled version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncThrottler` hook,\nproviding a stable, throttled async function reference for use in Preact components.\n\nThe throttled async function will execute at most once within the specified wait time period,\nregardless of how many times it is called. Calls made during the wait period reschedule a\nsingle trailing execution with the latest arguments when `trailing` is enabled (the default).\nThe most recent call's promise resolves or rejects with the trailing execution's result;\neach earlier call's promise resolves immediately with the most recent previous result (or\n`undefined` if nothing has executed yet), as does every call when the throttler is disabled.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncThrottler`, making it ideal for basic\nasync throttling needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncThrottler instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution/error state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncThrottler` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions`](../interfaces/PreactAsyncThrottlerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Throttle an async API call\nconst handleApiCall = useAsyncThrottledCallback(async (data) => {\n  const result = await sendDataToServer(data);\n  return result;\n}, {\n  wait: 200 // Execute at most once every 200ms\n});\n\n// Use in an event handler\n<button onClick={() => handleApiCall(formData)}>Send</button>\n```\n"}
